on.service.ts](/home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/agentic-federation-and-distribution-direction/apps/api/src/runs/run-execution.service.ts:419).\n\n## Important non-unification\n\nThe model-facing tool API remains separate from this Node protocol.\n\nA model may see `EnterWorkspace`; it must not receive a generic `execution.commands.submit` or `admin.*` client. The harness translates model tool calls into internal operations, applies permissions, and returns structured observations. This preserves the trusted harness boundary.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nHigh confidence:\n\n> Define one versioned llame Node Protocol with a mandatory `core` module and independently versioned, capability-negotiated `realm`, `execution`, `sync`, and `admin` modules. Local and hosted implementations share wire contracts and semantics, not storage, tenancy, framework, or complete capability sets. Direct access and tunnelling are interchangeable transports.\n\nDo you agree with this modular contract boundary, including `admin.*` being unavailable through ordinary tunnels by default?",
