ce-means-no-same-branch-failover rule are settled. Specify the placement,\\n-   checkpoint, barrier, prepare, compare-and-swap, acknowledgement, retry,\\n-   cancellation, and command-disposition schemas plus process-kill conformance\\n-   cases. Keep peer-hosted or movable fencing as later follow-ups until their\\n-   promotion trigger exists.\\n-2. **Enrollment and device-loss mechanics.** Disposable node identity,\\n-   OAuth-authorized enrollment, permanent cryptographic revocation, new-identity\\n-   relinking, and the limits of remote revocation are settled for the initial\\n-   contract. Specify platform key storage, enrollment confirmation, credential\\n-   renewal, revocation delivery, audit, and negative conformance cases. Keep\\n-   identity-preserving rotation, encrypted recovery, peer-distributed revocation,\\n-   hub-loss re-homing, and offline-authorship cutoffs as north-star follow-ups.\\n-3. **Personal Realm operational replication.** The authority map and storage-class\\n-   boundary are settled: trusted Personal Realm replicas may originate personal\\n-   state; Chats are database-native; every shared Space retains one governing\\n-   authority; every Chat or Run branch has a destination authority; and active\\n-   Run execution remains single-authority. Coverage must be explicit and cannot be\\n-   inferred from conflict absence. The semantic `ChangeBatch`, replication-journal,\\n-   and per-link delivery-state split is settled. Specify exact portable resource\\n-   schemas, authoritative snapshot and frontier mechanics, journal retention,\\n-   cursors, causal ordering, resumability, schema evolution, and per-resource\\n-   authorship plus merge/fork/proposal/rejection behavior. The capability-scoped\\n-   authorship north star, unified first-and-later reconciliation function,\\n-   snapshot-as-journal-prefix rule, three-layer active-Run durability boundary,\\n-   and the first-delivery resumable episodic record classes are settled; the\\n-   exact linked writer policy, causal ordering and fork behavior, schemas,\\n-   retention, artifact payload transport, and later mutable-resource protocols\\n-   remain open.\\n-4. **Execution module and tunnelling protocol.** Specify Run snapshot and live-delta\\n-   schemas, snapshot-revision handoff, direct and reverse-tunnel transports,\\n-   multiplexing, authorization, connection fencing, command idempotency and result\\n-   lookup, backpressure, and adapter conformance. Branch/session-scoped placement,\\n-   one current authority, epoch-targeted commands, executor-local raw mechanics,\\n-   fresh-snapshot reconnect recovery, executor-local journal versus portable\\n-   checkpoint separation, and rejection rather than relay queuing while offline\\n-   are settled. Also define how adapters advertise same-node process-recovery\\n-   guarantees without exposing provider-native journal schemas.\\n-5. **Workspace binding details.** Specify switching, archival, access-mode\\n-   changes, reauthorization, retention, availability detection and debounce, and\\n-   the exact recovery behavior for active versus not-yet-started Runs. Sticky\\n-   affinity and the four outage modes are settled.\\n-6. **Workspace registry privacy and liveness.** Define handle creation, path\\n-   redaction, labels, capability advertisement, online/offline state, stale\\n-   registrations, and what metadata each surface may see.\\n-7. **General permission model.** Extend `EnterWorkspace` into reusable scoped\\n-   `allow`/`ask`/`deny` rules, persistent approvals, revocation, audit, prompt\\n-   lifecycle, and separation among mount, filesystem, network, secret, device,\\n-   publish, and destructive-operation authority.\\n-8. **Sandbox-definition layering.** Decide which environment settings are global,\\n-   per user, per Agent Profile, per node, or per project; how candidate changes are\\n-   validated; and how accepted revisions, activation, rollback, and garbage\\n-   collection work.\\n-9. 